{{!--
  The loot card (D-721), in two modes and one template. Accent: gold.

  OFFERED - who is offering how many finds and what purse, to whom - carries
  the button that opens the shared window. SETTLED replaces it in place when
  the loot is handed over: the reason it ended, a line per character with
  @UUID links to what is now on their sheet, what was left behind, and what
  could not be found. It is ONE message either way, because the settle locks
  on the offer's own id (`keepId`), which is what stops a GM with two tabs
  handing the same find out twice.

  Every line is composed in `documents/loot-offer.mjs`. A line CARRYING A
  `@UUID[...]` mark is printed with a triple stash, as the feature card's bound
  lines are - core enriches the mark when the message renders, and an escaped
  stash would print its punctuation instead - and everything else takes the
  ordinary stash. What the composer splices into a triple-stashed line and the
  enricher does not own (a character's name, a find's name where its world copy
  has gone) is escaped there, because a name is a player's to type.
--}}
<div class="azeroth azeroth-card azeroth-card-loot" data-message-kind="{{kind}}">
  {{> systems/azeroth-rpg/templates/chat/partials/card-header.hbs title=title subtitle=subtitle}}

  <div class="azeroth-card-body">
    {{#if text}}<p class="azeroth-card-line azeroth-loot-offered">{{text}}</p>{{/if}}

    {{!-- WHO MAY OPEN THE WINDOW, on the card itself. The offered card is
          GM-authored, so `dice/chat.mjs`'s ownership rule would strip this
          from every player it is actually for; `data-offer-users` is what
          that module reads to keep it for the invited and take it from
          everybody else. A settled card has no window to open. --}}
    {{#if open}}
    <div class="azeroth-card-open" data-offer-users="{{userIds}}">
      <button type="button" data-offer-id="{{offerId}}" data-action="openLootOffer">{{localize "AZEROTH.LootOffer.Card.Open"}}</button>
    </div>
    {{/if}}

    {{#if reason}}<p class="azeroth-card-line azeroth-loot-reason">{{reason}}</p>{{/if}}

    {{#each lines}}
    <p class="azeroth-card-line azeroth-loot-gave">{{{this}}}</p>
    {{/each}}

    {{#if left.length}}
    <p class="azeroth-card-line azeroth-loot-left-label"><strong>{{leftLabel}}</strong></p>
    <ul class="azeroth-loot-left">
      {{#each left}}<li>{{{this}}}</li>{{/each}}
    </ul>
    {{/if}}

    {{!-- A note carries NO @UUID: it names a character or a find that could
          not be found, so it is an ordinary escaped stash. --}}
    {{#each notes}}
    <p class="azeroth-note azeroth-loot-note">{{this}}</p>
    {{/each}}
  </div>
</div>
